# config/provisioning.env — site provisioning defaults (TEMPLATE).
#
# Copy this file to config/provisioning.env (same directory) and fill in the
# values that are identical on EVERY box in your fleet. On a fresh install the
# first-boot wizard pre-fills each matching prompt with these values, so the
# technician just presses Enter to accept them (or types a different value to
# override). The only thing they must type per box is the site identity
# (district / school / device).
#
# Where to get these values:
#   Open the dashboard → Settings → SFTP ingestion → "Sensor auto-enrollment".
#   It shows your dashboard URL and the shared bootstrap key, and offers this
#   exact snippet to copy.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SECURITY — READ THIS
#   The bootstrap key is a SHARED SECRET. This repository is PUBLIC, so the
#   real file (config/provisioning.env) is git-ignored and must NEVER be
#   committed. Distribute it out-of-band (config-management, a golden image,
#   or a copy/paste over your own secure channel). Anyone holding the key can
#   enroll a sensor while auto-enrollment is enabled — rotate it from the
#   dashboard if it leaks.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# --- Dashboard control plane (same on every box) ---------------------------
# Outbound HTTPS only; the box opens no inbound ports. Leave both blank to run
# a box with no dashboard (SFTP-only).
NETMON_DASHBOARD_URL=https://netmon.example.org
NETMON_BOOTSTRAP_KEY=nmk_replace_me_with_the_key_from_the_dashboard

# --- Optional: shared SFTP drop --------------------------------------------
# If your whole fleet uploads to one SFTP destination, pre-fill it here too so
# the SFTP prompts are also Enter-to-accept. The password is a secret — set it
# here only if you accept storing it in this (out-of-band, non-committed) file;
# otherwise leave it out and the wizard will prompt for it.
#NETMON_SFTP_HOST=youraccount.blob.core.windows.net
#NETMON_SFTP_PORT=22
#NETMON_SFTP_USER=youraccount.sensor
#NETMON_SFTP_REMOTE_PATH=/
#NETMON_SFTP_PASSWORD=
